kind: llman.sdd.delta
ops[3]{op,req_id,title,statement,from,to,name}:
  add_requirement,r23,"xlsx spreadsheet books MUST use typed managed-artifact pipeline","When a workflow-managed demand output is bound to a shared book whose kind is `xlsx_file` or `xlsx_memory`, the system MUST materialize that output as `MANAGED_ARTIFACT_KIND_ROWS` (`InMemoryRows`) and MUST set the composed `OutputSpec.format` to `excel`. The pipeline MUST preserve `FieldValue` semantics (`int`/`float`/`Decimal`/`bool`/`str`/`None`) through write-node consumption and workbook/sheetbook planning, and MUST NOT first stringify via `InMemoryCsvSink` / `_normalize_csv_value()` for those book kinds. Write nodes for `resource_type=book` with xlsx kinds and legacy `resource_type=workbook` MUST resolve inputs via `resolve_workflow_input_tabular()`. At the final openpyxl append/export boundary, non-`str` values MUST be passed through (formula escaping applies to `str` only). `None` MUST NOT be converted to `''` solely because the destination is `xlsx_file`. Heuristic `_auto_cast` / guess-casting from strings MUST NOT be used to satisfy this requirement.",null,null,null
  add_requirement,r24,"ROWS managed plans MUST NOT eagerly duplicate CSV artifacts","For `ManagedArtifactPlan` with `kind=ROWS`, `_collect_managed_artifact_outputs()` MUST NOT call `to_csv_artifact()` / `in_memory_rows_to_in_memory_csv()` eagerly. This MUST apply to both `xlsx_file` and `xlsx_memory` managed outputs. `in_memory_rows_to_in_memory_csv()` MUST remain available as an explicit public utility. This requirement does NOT obligate the runtime to auto-derive CSV artifacts when a CSV consumer exists; any future consumer-driven derivation MUST be an explicit conversion (never unconditional eager duplication) and is out of scope for the change that introduces this requirement.",null,null,null
  add_requirement,r25,"xlsx_file workbook plans MUST own materialized typed row segments","`resources_workbook` MUST store sheet segments as owned typed rows (`List[List[FieldValue]]`) with `producer_node_id`, `decl_order`, and `header_policy`, materialized at `apply_workbook_sheet` / `apply_workbook_append` via `read_tabular_header` + alignment mapping + `materialize_aligned_tabular_rows`. Segments MUST NOT retain a parallel CSV input reference as the SSOT for commit. Commit/export MUST iterate owned segment rows and apply `escape_excel_formula` only to `str` values. `InMemoryCsv` and CSV file paths remain valid `WorkflowTabularInput` adapters at apply time, but after apply the plan SSOT is the materialized typed rows. Header/export_header/field_id alignment semantics MUST remain equivalent to the previous workbook behavior aside from value typing.",null,null,null
op_scenarios[10]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  r23,"xlsx-file-multi-sheet-preserves-numeric-types","a workflow with 3 runs writes three sheets to one `xlsx_file` book","workflow completes and the xlsx is loaded via openpyxl","numeric cells (amount/qty/price/rate/active/status) MUST be Python `int`/`float`/`bool`/`None` (not `str`)"
  r23,"xlsx-file-decimal-reaches-openpyxl-as-number","a demand field holds `Decimal(\"158.00\")` and writes to `xlsx_file` via workflow","workflow completes and the cell is read","the cell MUST NOT be the string `\"158.0\"`; it MUST be a numeric openpyxl value"
  r23,"xlsx-file-none-not-coerced-to-empty-string","a numeric field is `None` and writes to `xlsx_file` via workflow","workflow completes and the cell is inspected","the cell MUST be `None` (not `\"\"`)"
  r23,"xlsx-file-single-sheet-minimal-repro","a minimal 1-run 1-sheet workflow writes to `xlsx_file`","workflow completes","all covered numeric types in the sheet MUST remain typed"
  r23,"legacy-workbook-resource-type-uses-tabular-resolve","a write/append node uses legacy `resource_type=workbook`","the node resolves its input artifact","resolution MUST use the tabular path (accepting `InMemoryRows`), not CSV-only resolution"
  r24,"rows-plan-skips-eager-csv-copy","a ROWS `ManagedArtifactPlan` holds 100k rows × 9 cols","`_collect_managed_artifact_outputs` runs","no CSV copy MUST be created for that plan; only the rows artifact is published"
  r24,"csv-plan-still-emits-csv","a CSV `ManagedArtifactPlan` targets a csv/file output","`_collect_managed_artifact_outputs` runs","the CSV artifact MUST still be produced as before"
  r25,"workbook-apply-materializes-typed-rows","`apply_workbook_sheet` receives `InMemoryRows` with int/float/bool/None","apply completes","the workbook sheet segment MUST own materialized `FieldValue` rows (not a live CSV reference SSOT)"
  r25,"workbook-commit-writes-owned-typed-rows","a workbook plan has materialized typed segments","commit writes openpyxl","`ws.append` MUST receive the owned typed values after `escape_excel_formula` on strings only"
  r25,"workbook-still-accepts-incsv-adapter","`apply_workbook_sheet` receives `InMemoryCsv`","apply+commit succeed","behavior MUST remain valid; cell values MAY be strings because the adapter input was CSV-equivalent"
